{
  "borough": "Harrow",
  "application_type": "All Other",
  "decision": "Refused",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;p&gt;The proposed residential unit, by reason of its restricted floorspace below the required minimum gross internal area, would offer a substandard and cramped form of accommodation for future occupiers to the detriment of their living conditions. The development is thereby contrary to the high quality design aspirations of the National Planning Policy Framework (2024), Policies D3 and D6 of The London Plan (2021), Policy DM1 of the Harrow Development Management Policies Local Plan (2013); the adopted Supplementary Planning Documents Residential Design Guide (2010) and the Housing Design Standards LPG (2023).&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;The proposed rear roof dormer, due to its visual prominence, lack of setback from the northern roof edge, massing, is considered a bulky, cramped and poor quality feature that would fail to integrate with the original character of the property nor sit comfortably within the existing roofscape. This is considered contrary to the high-quality design aspirations of the National Planning Policy Framework (2024), Policy D3 Policy of the London Plan (2021); CS.1 of the Harrow Core Strategy (2012), Policy DM1 of the Development Management Plan Local Policies (2013) and the adopted Supplementary Planning Document: Residential Design Guide (2010).&lt;/p&gt;"
  ],
